{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1188670-using-fate-to-deal-with-cause-and-consequence","id":1188670,"title":"Using Fate to deal with Cause and Consequence","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-02-22T14:44:32-08:00","id":1188670,"title":"Using Fate to deal with Cause and Consequence","content":"I have been thinking a lot lately about using Fate in order to deal with Cause and Consequence, as well as Order and Chaos.<br /> I know neither of those are stated directly as the Arcanum\u00b4s purview (despite we getting a spell called &quot;Chaos Mastery&quot;), but I feel like Fate would deal nicely with those (in a sense, I think it already does), especially for a character with a more &quot;scientific&quot; understanding of the Arcanum.<br /> <br /> I was curious about how you would deal with a mage using Fate in order, for example, to find out a causal factor of something (eg: &quot;Was this cat the one who broke this vase?&quot; or maybe &quot;Is this factory\u00b4s pollution the cause of this person\u00b4s sickness?&quot;) or even divine a chain of effects (like the one established by a gossip- tracking back each element of the chain to its originator).<br /> Would you allow it? Keep in mind I understand such knowledge could be gained with other Arcana, it\u00b4s this specific use of Fate I\u00b4m concerned with.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3709-doktorniemand","name":"DoktorNiemand","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"48"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-22T15:09:29-08:00","id":1188676,"title":"","content":"I wouldn't allow it directly. Perhaps if you combined it with Temporal Sympathy (Time 2), you could design a spell which recreates the series of events as viewed through the lens of the Fate arcanum. But if you're already adding Time 2, you might as well just use Postcognition.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13082-projectmoon","name":"projectmoon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-22T18:40:25-08:00","id":1188736,"title":"","content":"Probably not.<br /> Fate doesn't care about most of the events that unfold in the universe.<br /> Only if there was some actual pattern, some fate for the cause to have resulted in the effect, would I say Fate could it detect the relationship.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12644-herbertisbestbert","name":"HerbertIsBestBert","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12644_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"312"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-22T20:53:10-08:00","id":1188767,"title":"","content":"I\u2019d say Fate only covers narrative causality, rather than \u2018scientific\u2019 causality. So a Fate spell telling you the cause of someone\u2019s death would say \u201che was a villain, avenged by the one he wronged.\u201d Meanwhile, Time would be the one telling you \u201che was stabbed with a knife.\u201d","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-22T21:37:51-08:00","id":1188774,"title":"","content":"It\u00b4s interesting to see the answers here are firmly in the &quot;nope&quot; camp. Maybe I\u00b4m misremembering how the old Entropy sphere worked? I always thought the chain of cause and effect would be something Fate would deal with. <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1188670-using-fate-to-deal-with-cause-and-consequence?p=1188767#post1188767\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I\u2019d say Fate only covers narrative causality, rather than \u2018scientific\u2019 causality. So a Fate spell telling you the cause of someone\u2019s death would say \u201che was a villain, avenged by the one he wronged.\u201d Meanwhile, Time would be the one telling you \u201che was stabbed with a knife.\u201d</div> </div> </div> </div>That\u00b4s interesting. Would you care to give a couple more examples? I don\u00b4t think I have a good grasp of how narrative causality would work in most games. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3709-doktorniemand","name":"DoktorNiemand","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"48"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-22T21:56:07-08:00","id":1188776,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DoktorNiemand</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1188670-using-fate-to-deal-with-cause-and-consequence?p=1188774#post1188774\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It\u00b4s interesting to see the answers here are firmly in the &amp;quot;nope&amp;quot; camp. Maybe I\u00b4m misremembering how the old Entropy sphere worked? I always thought the chain of cause and effect would be something Fate would deal with. </div> </div> </div> </div>\u201cSolid\u201d or \u201cobjective\u201d causality would be Time, at least in Awakening. No idea on the nuances and details of the Entropy and Time Spheres from Ascension. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> That\u00b4s interesting. Would you care to give a couple more examples? I don\u00b4t think I have a good grasp of how narrative causality would work in most games. </div> </div> </div>Q. Who broke this vase?<br /> A. Time: A cat just passed by 3 minutes and 2 seconds ago. <br /> Fate: The owner didn\u2019t care much for the vase, leaving it where anybody could bump into it. <br /> <br /> Q. Why is this person sick?<br /> A. Time: The factory upriver started to leak pollutants into the river 6 years and 8 days ago, which contaminated the tap water she drinks from.<br /> Fate: Greed and carelessness of the factory upriver led to the environment being damaged. <br /> <br /> Then again, as you noticed, this is a generous and broad reading of Fate\u2019s purviews on my side, unorthodox and not strictly canon unless future supplements end up backing me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-23T00:04:20-08:00","id":1188792,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DoktorNiemand</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1188670-using-fate-to-deal-with-cause-and-consequence?p=1188774#post1188774\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Maybe I\u00b4m misremembering how the old Entropy sphere worked?<br /> <br /> That\u00b4s interesting. Would you care to give a couple more examples? I don\u00b4t think I have a good grasp of how narrative causality would work in most games.</div> </div> </div> </div>In Awakening, you have Time, which describes what is most likely to/will happen (before you reading it changes it), and Fate, which describes what the Fate wants to happen.<br /> <br /> The Fate Arcanum, is by and large about getting Fate on your side so its delicate influence over the various forces of the cosmos align to bring about what you want to happen.<br /> Or with the later Practices, blowing the underlying principles out of the water and having SWAT teams smash their way through windows and angry Demigods awaken and conjure swarms of pestilence. I don't like the example spells for the later Practices.<br /> <br /> Fate doesn't care about everything, 'everything' is just the back-drop for 'something' to happen in.<br /> Fate might be able to tell you in great detail about the Destiny of a man's knife which is destined to bury itself in the eye-socket of an Angel.<br /> Or it might be able to tell you about the man who was destined to give his life for his son.<br /> <br /> But it cannot tell you the 'whys' about any game which Fate has no skin in.<br /> <br /> Time, is usually considered the 'information' Arcanum.<br /> With just 2 dots you can wind your perception back to the earliest parts of history.<br /> Go to the Pyramids of Egypt and you can use it to see thousands and thousands of years ago.<br /> <br /> Fate is very bad for telling you about anything but what is Fated.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12644-herbertisbestbert","name":"HerbertIsBestBert","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12644_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"312"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-23T02:22:26-08:00","id":1188807,"title":"","content":"You could however use Fate to set you up to find out how something happened, it just won\u2019t be as direct a revelation as a literal vision of the past.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-23T03:04:22-08:00","id":1188819,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HerbertIsBestBert</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1188670-using-fate-to-deal-with-cause-and-consequence?p=1188792#post1188792\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But it cannot tell you the 'whys' about any game which Fate has no skin in.<br /> <br /> Fate is very bad for telling you about anything but what is Fated.</div> </div> </div> </div>I strongly disagree with the entirety of this post, but I'll focus on this.<br /> <br /> Fate specifically has 'Intentions' within its purview. Imo, it is entirely reasonable for a Knowing Fate spell to reveal someone/something's intentions (the 'why' of something). Purviews exist for a reason and ignoring parts of them for vagueries (it's bad for anything but what's fated/destined/whatever) is not a good practice.<br /> <br /> That said, for the specific examples listed in OP - no, Time is going to be much better for most of those.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3570,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","user":"lnodiv","date":". 02-23-2018, 06:17 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-24T12:04:42-08:00","id":1189275,"title":"","content":"I like this question and I have thoughts on it...<br /> <br /> My opinion is formed from intensively playing an Acanthus character for a while and the way she approached Fate and Destiny and things like that.<br /> <br /> <b>Cause and Consquence</b> -- I'm reminded of the country song &quot;Third Rock From the Sun&quot; where the lyric says, &quot;cause and effect, chain of events, all of the chaos makes perfect sense!&quot; When another poster says Fate gives you a <i>narrative</i> understanding of things, I tend to say Fate give you an <i>intuitive</i> understanding of cause and consequence. If you're scientifically minded, then the entire universe is a random event in which Fate gives you some sort of insight into how things came to be and where they will likely go. If life was a Rube Goldberg machine, Fate can let you know Step A and Step Z, but you won't really be aware of all the little steps in between.<br /> <br /> This is why Fate covers <b>Intention</b>. This is why we have the spells <i>Interconnections, Reading the Outermost Eddies, Serendipity</i> and the like. That's just Fate 1. Awareness. <br /> <br /> That's one of the things that I found fascinating about playing an Acanthus character: having this awareness to understand the consequence of actions, of choices, of inaction. It makes you seem like a crazy person because you do things with no seeming logic behind them. You put money into a vending machine, but don't buy anything. You wait to cross the street until the third time the crosswalks signals that it's safe to walk. You sit at a red light instead of going. You choose the red shirt instead of the blue one that day. Things like that.<br /> <br /> I might agree that Fate won't tell you the whys of something, but I would say that's because it doesn't matter why. It just matters. &quot;Whatever you do: don't get on that 3:30 flight...I've got a bad feeling.&quot; Stuff like that. It can become an Obsession, being superstitious or paranoid. What if you imagined that other people know the things you know or have your awareness... then there's no such thing as accidents and random chance. <i>Things happen because people choose to make them happen.</i> What if you have a twisted sense of justice or a vindictive personality? Bad news for people who cross you and don't even know why.<br /> <br /> This harkens back to the Euthanatoi and the old Entropy Sphere of magic.<br /> <br /> Does that make sense?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/346-troy","name":"Troy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"293"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}